.TH WB\-VIEW 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-view \- show what a session of a role sees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR view <issue> (<role> [\-\-in | \-\-out] | <path>)
.br
or \-\-kept [\-v | \-\-verbose]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Show what a session of a role will see, before it starts. wb view <issue> <role> prints the paths of its view, one to a line, the list the start makes the view from, and nothing else. \-\-in [<folder>] prints what of HEAD the view holds in the folder (the root when none is given), one level deep: each file in it, and <count><tab><folder>/ for each folder below it.
.PP
\-\-out prints the same for what the view leaves out. A folder is a path from the root, with or without a closing /. The level and the line view: are in wb prompt <role> <issue> \-\-stamp.
.PP
wb view <issue> <path> says for each role whether the path, from the root, is in its view: in, with the list and the line of the issue's file that hold it, or out, and why. A path named as a role is written ./<path>. Ends with 0 when the path is in the view of a role or the view is shown, 1 when it is in none, the folder is not in HEAD or the issue has no accepted, committed file, 2 when it was used wrongly (a file given as the folder too) or the repository is not set up.
.PP
wb view \-\-kept takes no other word but \-v. It lists the views kept on this machine for this repository whose session does not run, one to a line: the folder, the role, round <n>, issue <issue>, and <k> commits not taken <m> paths uncommitted, or not read where git could not read the view. \-v (\-\-verbose) adds below each line why it was kept, each commit not taken, each path left uncommitted, and why a view was not read. It writes nothing.
.PP
Writes nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-in [<folder>]
Print what of HEAD the view holds in the folder (the root when none is given), one level deep: each file in it, and <count><tab><folder>/ for each folder below it.
.TP
.B \-\-out
Print the same for what the view leaves out. A folder is a path from the root, with or without a closing /.
.TP
.B \-\-kept
List the views kept on this machine for this repository, with what is left in each.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
With \-\-kept, add below each line why the view was kept, each commit not taken, each path left uncommitted, and why a view was not read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The path is in the view of a role, or the view is shown.
.TP
.B 1
The path is in none, the folder is not in HEAD, or the issue has no accepted, committed file.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly (a file given as the folder too) or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
